<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	Intentionally empty for now. LilPasswordsAgent stores the vault key in the
	legacy file-based Keychain (kSecUseDataProtectionKeychain = false), which
	needs no entitlement at all — see docs/adr/0001-storage-and-process-model.md.

	Do NOT add keychain-access-groups here without also provisioning it: it's a
	restricted entitlement, and AMFI SIGKILLs a process that carries it without
	a matching provisioning profile from the signing team (confirmed empirically
	while writing the ADR above). That profile doesn't exist until the 851 Labs
	Apple Developer team is set up (851-2400).

	XPC (851-2427) will likely add a MachServices key to the agent's launchd
	plist (Agent/Support/com.851labs.lilpasswords.agent.plist), not an
	entitlement here — Mach service lookup by an unsandboxed client needs no
	entitlement.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
